# Normalise line endings so a checkout is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks out CRLF (core.autocrlf defaults to true
# there), Prettier's endOfLine is "lf", and `npm run format:check` fails on
# EVERY file in the repository. The Windows CI job flagged 102 of them the
# first time it ran — which is what a contributor on Windows would have seen
# on their first command, with nothing in the output to suggest the cause was
# line endings rather than their own change.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree as well as in the repository, so the
# checked-out bytes match what CI, Prettier and ESLint all expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and generated artifacts: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.skill binary
*.tgz binary
*.zip binary

# The schema fixture is generated output committed verbatim. It is LF by the
# rule above, which is correct — but it must never be reformatted, and
# .prettierignore already excludes it.
tests/fixtures/*.json -diff

# Lockfiles are noisy in review and machine-owned.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
